==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|incounter||archaic}}
* {{alter|en|encountre|incountre||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|encountren}}, from rom {{etyl|xno|en}} {{m|fro|encountrer}}, {{etyl|fro|en}} {{m|fro|encontrer||to confront}}, from {{m|fro|encontre||against, counter to}}, from {{etyl|LL.|en}} {{m|la|incontrā||in front of}} itself from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|in||in}} + {{m|la|contrā||against}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈkaʊntɚ/|/ɪŋˈkaʊntɚ/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ɪnˈkaʊntə/|/ɪŋˈkaʊntə/}}
* {{hyph|en|en|coun|ter}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-encounter.ogg|Audio (US)}}
* {{rhymes|en|aʊntə(ɹ)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[meet]] (someone) or find (something), especially [[unexpectedly]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[confront]] (someone or something) face to face.
# {{lb|en|ambitransitive}} To [[engage]] in [[conflict]], as with an enemy.
#: ''Three armies '''encountered''' at Waterloo.''
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Titus|V|ii|passage=I will '''encounter''' with Andronicus.}}

